# 5. How Mirage should handle OpenAI `tools`

When a client sends:

```json
{
  "tools": [
    {
      "type": "function",
      "function": {
        "name": "write_file",
        "description": "Write a file",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "name": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "content": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          "required": ["name", "content"]
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

Mirage should do this internally:

```text
1. Accept OpenAI tools from client
2. Normalize them into MirageToolDefinition
3. Compile them into prompt text
4. Strip tools from upstream provider request if nativeTools=false
5. Send prompt to internal provider API
6. Parse response for MTP blocks
7. Convert MTP blocks back into OpenAI tool_calls
```

---

## Canonical tool definition

```ts
type MirageToolDefinition = {
  name: string;
  description?: string;
  parameters: {
    type: "object";
    properties: Record<string, unknown>;
    required?: string[];
  };
};
```

All provider/tool logic should operate on this canonical shape.

