# 8. Do not forward native tools upstream by default

For browser/internal endpoints, your default should be:

```ts
stripUpstreamTools: true
```

Why?

Because your test shows:

```text
tools parameter alone = ignored
```

And worse, native tool payloads can:

- trigger unsupported provider behavior
- confuse product tool routing
- leak into built-in tools
- cause malformed streaming
- break OpenCode integration
- make the model think it should use hidden provider tools

So Mirage should translate:

```json
{
  "tools": [...]
}
```

into prompt instructions instead.

