# 13. Converting MTP to OpenAI tool_calls

When Mirage gets a valid MTP block:

```json
{
  "id": "call_001",
  "name": "write_file",
  "arguments": {
    "name": "hello.txt",
    "content": "Hello, world!"
  }
}
```

Convert it to OpenAI format:

```json
{
  "id": "call_001",
  "type": "function",
  "function": {
    "name": "write_file",
    "arguments": "{\"name\":\"hello.txt\",\"content\":\"Hello, world!\"}"
  }
}
```

Important:

OpenAI expects `function.arguments` to be a JSON string, not an object.

So:

```ts
const openAIToolCall = {
  id: mtpCall.id ?? generateToolCallId(),
  type: "function",
  function: {
    name: mtpCall.name,
    arguments: JSON.stringify(mtpCall.arguments ?? {})
  }
};
```

If the model does not provide `id`, generate one:

```ts
function generateToolCallId() {
  return `call_${Math.random().toString(36).slice(2, 12)}`;
}
```

