# 16. Tool result messages must be normalized

Clients will send back:

```json
{
  "role": "tool",
  "tool_call_id": "call_001",
  "content": "File written successfully"
}
```

But your internal browser APIs probably do not understand `role: "tool"`.

So Mirage must convert it.

For upstream, convert tool result into a user message:

```text
[MIRAGE_TOOL_RESULT_V1]
{
  "id": "call_001",
  "output": "File written successfully",
  "error": null
}
[/MIRAGE_TOOL_RESULT_V1]

Continue the conversation based on this tool result.
```

Similarly, if there is an assistant message with OpenAI `tool_calls`, convert it into assistant text:

```text
[MIRAGE_TOOL_CALL_V1]
{
  "id": "call_001",
  "name": "write_file",
  "arguments": {
    "name": "hello.txt",
    "content": "Hello, world!"
  }
}
[/MIRAGE_TOOL_CALL_V1]
```

This keeps the conversation coherent for providers that do not support native tool roles.

