# 19. File upload support

You want major OpenAI features, including file upload.

For Mirage, file upload must be provider-specific.

Do not build one universal file uploader and expect it to work.

Build a file adapter interface.

---

## Canonical file object

```ts
type MirageFile = {
  id: string;
  filename: string;
  mimeType: string;
  size: number;
  source: {
    type: "base64" | "url" | "local";
    data?: string;
    url?: string;
  };
  providerFileId?: string;
};
```

---

## Provider upload adapter

```ts
interface ProviderFileAdapter {
  upload(file: MirageFile): Promise<{
    providerFileId: string;
  }>;

  attachToRequest(
    request: any,
    files: MirageFile[]
  ): Promise<any>;
}
```

---

## Upload flow

```text
Client uploads file to Mirage
        ↓
Mirage stores temporary file
        ↓
Provider adapter uploads file to internal provider API
        ↓
Provider returns internal file ID
        ↓
Mirage stores mapping
        ↓
Chat request includes provider-specific attachment field
```

Do not rely on the model reading file contents unless the provider API supports it.

If provider has no upload API:

- fallback to text extraction
- fallback to base64 if supported
- fallback to markdown description
- or mark model as no-file-support

