# 20. Reverse-engineering internal APIs correctly

You said:

> ALWAYS PREFER THE ACTUAL BACKGROUND API, NOT CHAT AUTOMATION.

This is correct.

Use browser automation only for capture/session, not as the runtime path.

---

## Use Obscura/browser to capture

For each provider, capture:

1. login/session flow
2. model selection request
3. chat completion request
4. streaming format
5. file upload request
6. CSRF headers
7. cookies
8. auth tokens
9. rate-limit headers
10. error shapes

Prefer HAR export.

Then convert the captured request into an adapter.

---

## Adapter should describe the real API

Example:

```ts
const deepseekAdapter = {
  endpoint: "https://chat.deepseek.com/api/v1/chat/completions",
  method: "POST",
  headers: {
    authorization: "Bearer {accessToken}",
    "x-csrf-token": "{csrfToken}"
  },
  body: {
    model: "{model}",
    messages: "{messages}",
    stream: true
  },
  streamFormat: "sse"
};
```

But in practice, many internal APIs are weird.

So adapters will need custom code.

That is unavoidable.

