# 22. OpenCode integration

If Mirage models behave weirdly in OpenCode, the issue is likely that OpenCode is trying to use native tool calling directly against Mirage endpoints.

The fix:

> OpenCode should talk to Mirage as if Mirage is an OpenAI API.  
> Mirage should handle the internal tool translation.

OpenCode should not know that the upstream provider is broken.

So:

```text
OpenCode
  ↓
OpenAI-compatible Mirage endpoint
  ↓
Mirage converts tools internally
```

If OpenCode has provider settings like:

```text
supportsTools = true
```

you can keep that enabled because Mirage’s public API supports tools.

But internally Mirage must not forward those tools to broken providers.

