# 28. What not to do

Do not build a giant agent framework.

Do not make every provider custom without shared types.

Do not rely on model “being smart”.

Do not send native tools to providers that ignore them.

Do not parse tool calls only after the full response if you want streaming.

Do not allow arbitrary built-in tool names to execute.

Do not use complex JSON Schema dumps for weak models.

Do not create ten different tool formats unless profile-driven.

Do not make XML and MTP two completely separate codepaths.

Use one core pipeline and pluggable dialects.

