# 30. The most important rule

Your test gave you the answer:

> The upstream browser/internal APIs are not reliable native tool-calling endpoints.

So Mirage must become a translator:

```text
OpenAI tool calling outside
Mirage prompted tool output inside
Provider internal API underneath
```

That is the production-grade design.

It is fast because you stream and only buffer tool blocks.

It is robust because you validate and repair.

It is strong because provider profiles handle quirks.

It avoids manual redundancy because the conformance suite and adapter SDK do the heavy lifting.

And it fixes the fundamental brokenness:

> Mirage does not ask broken providers to “call tools natively”.  
> Mirage asks them to output tool calls in a controlled format, then Mirage converts those into native OpenAI tool calls.